# Cross-origin isolation.
#
# SharedArrayBuffer — which the judge uses to interrupt a testcase that
# outruns its wall-clock deadline — is only exposed to cross-origin isolated
# documents. Without these two headers the constructor is simply undefined and
# judging silently falls back to adjudicating the deadline after each testcase
# has already run to completion.
#
# require-corp blocks cross-origin subresources that do not opt in. This site
# serves Pyodide, the WASM modules and every asset from its own origin. Verified
# by serving this file through Cloudflare's local runtime (`pnpm preview:cf`):
# both headers present, crossOriginIsolated true, SharedArrayBuffer available,
# no blocked subresource. `vitepress dev` does NOT send these — a declaration in
# the Vite config was measured to have no effect — so deadline behaviour must be
# checked under `pnpm preview:cf`, never under the dev server.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
